e um the policies and the  strategies that are needed to grow our  economy and that's the focus of Kia  stalma's speech today of how we're going  to actually grow our economy because  over the last 10 years or so the economy  has flatlined with growth bumping along  next year there are growth forecasts say  that we are going to have the slowest  growth in the G20 apart from Russia and  that we're going to have the highest  inflation in the G7 and that is  disastrous for the British economy it's  the worst of Both Worlds where you have  inflation high and rising and growth low  and falling we've got to get out of this  vicious spiral and actually have a  serious plan for boosting growth and  that's what Kia's speaking about today  okay so what would you do about a  National Insurance increase would you  scrap it  oh when we had the National Insurance uh  increase uh proposals come to Parliament  labor MPS voted against it Rishi sunak  introduced it and Liz Charles voted for  it Liz trust is now a convert to our way  of thinking which was to say that  National Insurance contribution  increases was the wrong tax at the wrong  time right in the middle of a cost of  living crisis so we wouldn't have had  the National Insurance contribution  increase yeah but if people lost raising  12 billion quid a year isn't it for  social care in the NHS so where would  that money come from  well the the they the the chancellor got  rid of half of his uh increase in  National Insurance contributions so it  wouldn't raise uh quite that amount of  money but it doesn't seem right to me uh  that it is almost working people under  the conservatives that are bearing the  burden of Taxation it's why I've set out  some targeted tax increases on the very  wealthy so we've said that we would  abolish the non-dom tax status because  if you make Britain your home you should  pay your taxes here we've said that if  you're a private Equity boss your  bonuses should be treated as income and  not as 